		{
			"id": 2032168,
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://c.im/@cwilcox808/117271169812130790",
			"author": {
				"name": "Curtis Wilcox",
				"url": "https://c.im/@cwilcox808",
				"avatarUrl": "https://avatars.webmention.io/cdn.masto.host/0420c3d68553f90b79bc3a720f1602dddc548654d07adad891d1cd66432ae2ce.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2026-09-14T20:00:43.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> <br />You bet. 👍</p><p>On your site, I noticed that when CSS is turned off, the word \"Auto\" is always displayed, regardless of state.</p><p>Also,  the solar eclipse toggle doesn't do anything visible while CSS is off , the site uses whatever `prefers-color-scheme` says. This makes sense to me and perhaps the button could reflect that. <br />If you wanted it to do something visible, you could make it edit the content in &lt;meta name=\"color-scheme\"&gt; to force a color-scheme.</p>",
			"type": "reply",
			"via": "webmention"
		},
		{
			"id": 2032404,
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/sarcevic.dev/post/3mvkuntq2ns2d",
			"author": {
				"name": "toni / link",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/sarcevic.dev",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:hi2as635pg63iytfw53yvnjl/bafkreihp44tsuws2krifwwpbqkizxfirimawraapdlczvc6xl2mu2xeawu"
			},
			"date": "2026-09-15T14:49:15.000Z",
			"content": "in case you want more feedback 😅<br>\nimo the separator makes it a bit ambiguous to what &quot;Auto&quot; is referring to, and i first read it like the toggle thinks the current selection is Auto, but it&apos;s for switching _to_ light/auto. maybe (auto) in quotes without separator would work better?",
			"type": "reply",
			"via": "webmention"
		},
		{
